Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Young Tableaux and Tensor Symmetries", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"e9ff11e1-8560-4d9f-a358-bfb444e19906"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The symmetric group ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["S", "n"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "71614702-ed33-4448-a715-04af0725eb1a"],
 " acts on a rank-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["n", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "34aba0ad-135d-468c-87c7-89a2e9864979"],
 " tensor by permuting its slots, and the resulting representation splits \
into a direct sum of irreducibles labelled by Young tableaux. The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Wolfram`TensorNetworks`Symmetry`",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/guide/TensorNetworks"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"907b0fc3-8aae-4c06-9944-fa567b50d516"],
 " subpackage exposes the combinatorial layer (tableaux, hook lengths, \
dimensions) together with the projectors that decompose a tensor into its \
irreducible pieces. This tutorial walks through the data structure, the \
hook-length formula, and the Young projector on small explicit examples."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b200f727-a7d2-452e-96b3-b5c078037cf5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`TensorNetworks`\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:=",ExpressionUUID->"116f07b5-33f4-46ab-be2d-cdfe4bb61bd2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`TensorNetworks`Symmetry`\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.988224958096567*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[3]:=",ExpressionUUID->"be00c723-bc95-4a28-8fce-b560869cf386"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Young Tableaux and Symmetry Classes", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ce9e72c8-db2f-4140-aaaf-534dc7434dfb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A Young diagram of size ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["n", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "884ab584-e49c-48a0-8eb9-3275dd463256"],
 " is a partition of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["n", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ce91ebaf-3a79-4831-bd54-10a8080ae7ff"],
 " into rows of non-increasing length, drawn as a left-justified array of \
boxes. Filling those boxes with the slot indices ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", " ", "n"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"f7d504c6-60c1-4a75-a3f4-63c6fd186492"],
 " gives a standard Young tableau, which the paclet stores as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["YoungTableau",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/YoungTableau"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"98ccfb26-bd57-4416-ab83-707a9b1035b0"],
 ". Every standard tableau labels an irreducible representation of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["S", "n"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "585538fa-3eed-453b-b857-e5f53f280090"],
 " acting on rank-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["n", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "b1fa92dd-ee26-4d23-b1ca-35a3db0ea4dd"],
 " tensors."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1d96e511-1452-4347-aed7-13cb866a6b41"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two extremes are familiar. The single-row shape ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", "n", "}"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "f6690bcf-8d07-4011-9fca-f8b0d4ff4dba"],
 " corresponds to the fully symmetric tensors, the single-column shape ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "1", ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", "1"}], "}"}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1feece62-4224-4d5b-ab9a-dda9eebaa4b7"],
 " to the fully antisymmetric ones, and the mixed shapes label all the \
intermediate irreps. The constructor accepts either an explicit filling or \
just a partition (auto-filled left-to-right, top-to-bottom)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ab1186ac-2480-4855-9230-f2de1bb9edea"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"yt", "=", 
  RowBox[{"YoungTableau", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"3", ",", "2"}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.988224985520213*^9, 3.988225001760675*^9}, {
  3.9882250594090137`*^9, 3.9882250600689287`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[4]:=",
